# CVE-2026-22732 (spring-security-web): fix requires spring-security-web >=6.5.9,
# which needs Spring Framework 6.2+ (i.e. Spring Boot 3.5.x+). Spring Boot 3.3.x and
# Spring Security 6.3.x are both past their patch window, so no backport exists.
# Remove this line once the project is upgraded to Spring Boot 3.5.x or later.
CVE-2026-22732

# CVE-2026-47884 (spring-webmvc): RCE/SSRF in XsltView. Only exploitable if the app
# renders views via XsltView with a "/**" mapping and no explicit view name — this is
# a REST-only API (@RestController, no XSLT/view rendering anywhere), so not reachable.
# OSS fix is Spring Framework 7.0.9 (Spring Boot 4.x); 6.1.29 is Enterprise Support
# only, so no OSS backport exists on the 6.1.x line.
# Remove this line once the project is upgraded to Spring Boot 4.x.
CVE-2026-47884
